cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use BGC-TFBS, please cite the dataset record below and, once it is
  out, the accompanying paper.
type: software
title: "BGC-TFBS: conserved regulatory motifs in biosynthetic gene clusters"
abstract: >-
  A web resource for exploring pathway-specific transcription factors and
  upstream regulatory motifs across gene cluster families derived from the
  BiG-FAM database, with sequence-similarity networks of 20 transcription
  factor families and comparison of de-novo motifs against PRODORIC.
authors:
  - family-names: Matine
    given-names: Idris
    affiliation: >-
      Qsys Lab, Centre for Host-Microbiome Interactions, King's College London
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-15"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sysbiomelab/BGC-TFBS"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22766286
    description: The full dataset (Zenodo record 22766286)
keywords:
  - biosynthetic gene clusters
  - transcription factor binding sites
  - regulatory motifs
  - MEME
  - PRODORIC
  - BiG-FAM
